xnu 0306: the Settings app can be watched from inside

Tapping General > Date & Time in the Settings app marks the row and then nothing
happens: the pane never arrives, the app's main thread sits idle in
CFRunLoopRun, and the list stops taking further touches. Measured with the
process sampler: the same is true with the GL shim forced onto its CPU copy path
(glcopy=1), so the renderer is not the reason, and the SystemConfiguration
thread seen earlier exists before the row is ever touched. What is left is the
app's own decision: PSListController pushes nothing when it cannot resolve the
specifier's detail class, and only the process can say which of the two happened.

mondrian_probe=1 injects /private/var/vm/mondrian-probe.dylib into the app named
by mondrian_probe_proc (default Preferences) and prints three things to the
console ring: the classes the pane needs at load, the row and detail class of
every selection, and the controller every showController:animated: is given
("nil" included). A selection with no showController, or a showController with
nil, is the answer; a real controller that never becomes visible moves the
question to the controller's own view load.

The dylib travels the way the UI hook does (0264): glblob=1 writes it out of the
kernel image into /private/var/vm, so a probe change costs one kernel build and
one `fastboot boot` rather than a userdata flash. Without glblob or without the
file the injection is refused and the boot is unchanged. tools/gen-glblob.py
takes it as an optional fourth input and the Linux build passes it when
out/gpu/mondrian-probe.dylib exists; tools/build-mondrian-probe.sh builds it
(tools/mondrian-probe.c).

--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5674,6 +5674,41 @@
 	}
 	return true;
 }
+/*
+ * mondrian_probe=1 injects /private/var/vm/mondrian-probe.dylib into one named
+ * app (mondrian_probe_proc, default "Preferences"), so a pane that does nothing
+ * can be explained from inside the process: a row that selects but never pushes
+ * means the specifier's controller class did not resolve, and only the app can
+ * say which. glblob=1 writes that file out of the kernel image at boot, so
+ * watching a build costs one kernel build and one `fastboot boot`.
+ */
+static bool
+mondrian_probe_env(struct image_params *imgp, char *env, size_t size)
+{
+	int enabled = 0;
+	char proc[32];
+	const char *name;
+	const char probe[] = "DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES=/private/var/vm/mondrian-probe.dylib";
+
+	if (!PE_parse_boot_argn("mondrian_probe", &enabled, sizeof(enabled)) ||
+	    !enabled || imgp->ip_ndp == NULL) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	if (!PE_parse_boot_argn("mondrian_probe_proc", proc, sizeof(proc))) {
+		strlcpy(proc, "Preferences", sizeof(proc));
+	}
+	name = imgp->ip_ndp->ni_cnd.cn_nameptr;
+	if (name == NULL || sizeof(probe) > size) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	if (imgp->ip_ndp->ni_cnd.cn_namelen != strlen(proc) ||
+	    strncmp(name, proc, strlen(proc)) != 0) {
+		return false;
+	}
+	strlcpy(env, probe, size);
+	return true;
+}
+
 #endif
 
